{#
  VRTouchEvents - AFTER THE CHOKE.                  (2026-09-12, the user's design)

  The choke block (0796) did its job, and now her last few turns are choked noise
  sitting in the context window - and the model goes on imitating what it sees.
  VRTE recorded exactly this failure in August, at StartChoke: a "cannot speak"
  event "lingered in her context and swallowed the RELEASE reaction too, leaving
  her silent even after letting go." Withdrawing a constraint does not delete the
  turns it already produced, so the release gets its own block for as long as
  those turns are still in view:

      moderate   a 3-7s choke    2 renders
      severe     a 7-15s choke   3 renders - the body came close to giving out

  A 1-3s squeeze never raised the choke block, so it needs no recovery.

  ★★★★ THE GATE IS THE LIVE STATE FILE (2026-09-12, fourth design - see 0796): read_json of
  VRTouchEvents/prompt_state, state 2 (moderate, a 3-7s choke) or 3 (severe, 7-15s), written by
  VRTouchEvents.dll at the release BEFORE the release narration, so her reply to it is the first
  render to carry this block. (The third design gated on get_faction_rank; SkyrimNet's view of a
  faction lags ~20 s - the block only showed on a reply 20 min later in VR test 4.) It comes off after her 2 / 3 SPOKEN replies - counted by
  VRTouchEvents.dll from SkyrimNet's "dialogue" event - or after 180 s, whichever first.
  One faction, one rank: being choked again sets rank 1, so this block and 0796 can never
  render together.

  ★ ENFORCE, DO NOT NEGATE. This block's whole job is to stop an imitation, so it
    must never print the thing to imitate. Every line names what IS true.
  ★ FACTUAL, per the user: the after-state of the BODY only - pain, the lingering
    press of the fingers, and for severe the near-passout disorientation. How she
    takes it, and what she says, is the LLM's to play.
  ⚠ A faction rank is a real number (a non-member reads below 0) - no isString guard needed.

  History: the Papyrus-decorator version never rendered once (its cache entry had expired by
  her next reply), and the C++-decorator version was reused by SkyrimNet for ~30 s. And both
  headings set the
  name into a variable before upper-casing it: filtering decnpc(npc.UUID).name directly printed
  the raw expression into her prompt.
  ★★★★★ THE CACHE-BUST (2026-09-13, VR test 5 + the user). SkyrimNet caches EVERY template call by name + argument
  value (55 s default, 30 s from a voice key press), so a plain read_json of this file was served stale on 2 of 7
  renders - the modified-time check inside read_json never runs on a cache hit. The second argument is three
  fresh random values (random is never cached): a number, so read_json ignores it and returns the whole file
  (SkyrimNet.dll 0x697500 - a path is used only when that argument is a string), but it is part of the cache key,
  so nearly every render is a new key and a real read. VERIFIED LIVE 2026-09-13 20:45 (VR test 8, report 45): the DLL wrote the state, the
  render 189 ms later logged 'File modified since cached, reloading' and this block was in that prompt; 22 of 22
  renders in the session ran the read (0 served stale by the callback cache).
  To revert: drop the second argument.
  ★ GAG + THOUGHTS (2026-09-13, fix list 41 V6, the user: "V6 yes"). A GAGGED NPC gets no recovery block: DD SN's
  0795 tells the LLM every sound she makes is raw voice only, and this block's "every reply from here is spoken aloud,
  in words" rendered two files later overrode the gag for 2-3 renders. The gate is the same native keyword test as
  0795 and DD SN's 0791 - zad_DeviousGag, plus ZaZ's zbfWornGag and Diary of Mine's DOMWornGag, which 0795 also
  renders for through its name decorator. (worn_has_keyword on a keyword a load order lacks reads false - SkyrimNet's
  own prompts test DD and SLA keywords for every user.) And no render in thoughts: "spoken aloud" is noise there.
#}
{% if render_mode != "thoughts" and exists("npc") and existsIn(npc, "UUID") %}
{% set _vs = read_json("VRTouchEvents/prompt_state", random * 10000 + random * 100 + random) %}
{% set _vc_rank = 0 %}
{% if isObject(_vs) and existsIn(_vs, "npcs") %}{% for _ve in _vs.npcs %}{% if _ve.uuid == npc.UUID %}{% set _vc_rank = _ve.state %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
{% if (_vc_rank == 2 or _vc_rank == 3) and not worn_has_keyword(npc.UUID, "zad_DeviousGag") and not worn_has_keyword(npc.UUID, "zbfWornGag") and not worn_has_keyword(npc.UUID, "DOMWornGag") %}
{% set _p = "he" %}{% set _pp = "his" %}{% set _po = "him" %}
{% if decnpc(npc.UUID).isFemale %}{% set _p = "she" %}{% set _pp = "her" %}{% set _po = "her" %}{% endif %}
{% set _vc_name = decnpc(npc.UUID).name %}
{% if _vc_rank == 3 %}
**THE CHOKE IS OVER - {{ _vc_name | upper }} SPEAKS AGAIN, PULLED BACK FROM THE EDGE OF PASSING OUT.** The hand is off {{ _pp }} throat and {{ _pp }} voice is {{ _pp }} own again, raw and hoarse. Every reply from here is spoken aloud, in words.

{{ _pp | capitalize }} body came within seconds of giving out. The throat is raw and bruised and burns with every breath. {{ _pp | capitalize }} head swims and the edges of {{ _pp }} vision still flicker dark, so {{ _p }} is disoriented and confused, slow to take hold of what is happening around {{ _po }}. The press of fingers still lingers on {{ _pp }} neck.

How {{ _p }} takes what was just done to {{ _po }}, and what {{ _p }} says, follows from who {{ _p }} is.
{% else %}
**THE CHOKE IS OVER - {{ _vc_name | upper }} SPEAKS AGAIN.** The hand is off {{ _pp }} throat and {{ _pp }} voice is {{ _pp }} own again, hoarse at first. Every reply from here is spoken aloud, in words.

{{ _pp | capitalize }} throat aches and throbs where the grip crushed it, each breath rasps a little on the way in, and the press of fingers still lingers on {{ _pp }} neck.

How {{ _p }} takes what was just done to {{ _po }}, and what {{ _p }} says, follows from who {{ _p }} is.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
